{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"As of November 6, 2026, [Rule 6c-11(b)](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-270.6c-11) provides qualifying ETFs four categories of conditional relief:\n\n1. **Creation-unit redemptions:** Shares qualify as redeemable securities although individually nonredeemable.\n2. **Market-price trading:** Secondary-market transactions may occur at negotiated market prices rather than NAV.\n3. **Affiliate basket transactions:** In-kind deposits and withdrawals are permitted with affiliates whose affiliation arises solely from specified ETF-share ownership or ownership-based control relationships. This is **not blanket permission** for transactions with advisers or affiliates connected for other reasons.\n4. **Delayed foreign-investment delivery:** Redemption delivery may exceed the usual seven-day limit when foreign-market holidays or extended settlement cycles prevent timely delivery. Delivery must occur **as soon as practicable, and no later than 15 days** after tender.\n\n**Worth knowing:** The foreign-delivery exception does not authorize a routine 15-day redemption period."}}
